      "widgets_values": [
        "## Dials, in the order you should touch them\n\n**1. `steps` (Scheduler node).** Every step streams the full 21 GB DiT. Step count is\ndirectly proportional to wall-clock time. 20 is the quality default; 12-14 is fine for\nchecking framing and motion before committing.\n\n**2. `Duration`.** 2.0 s -> 56 frames. The math node snaps seconds *up* to H3's 17k+5\nframe grid at 24 fps, so the value you type is a request, not the result - only these\nlengths are reachable, and anything in between rounds up to the next one:\n\n| you set | frames | real length | latent T |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1.0 | 39 | 1.62 s | 12 |\n| 2.0 | 56 | 2.33 s | 17 |\n| 2.5 or 3.0 | 73 | 3.04 s | 22 |\n| 3.5 | 90 | 3.75 s | 27 |\n| 4.0 | 107 | 4.46 s | 32 |\n| 4.5 or 5.0 | 124 | 5.17 s | 37 |\n\n**3. `Resolution`.** Note this barely moves VRAM - the weights dominate, not the\nactivations. It moves *compute* time. H3 is trained on a 768 px short edge capped at\n768x1344, so going below 768 costs real quality for modest speed. Settings that land\nexactly on native canvases (keep `multiple` = 32):\n\n| aspect | megapixels | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1:1 | 0.56 | 768 x 768 (default here) |\n| 4:3 | 0.75 | 1024 x 768 |\n| 3:4 | 0.75 | 768 x 1024 |\n| 16:9 | 0.98 | 1344 x 768 |\n| 9:16 | 0.98 | 768 x 1344 |\n\n1344x768 at 5 s is the heavy end - ~37k tokens through the DiT. It fits in 8 GB but\nit is where you would first see an OOM if something else is on the GPU.\n\n**4. `Sigma Shift`.** 12.0 / 3.0 are exactly the model's built-in defaults, so the node\nis a no-op as wired. It is here purely so you have the knob. Lower `shift_video`\nfor tighter, less drifty motion.\n\n**5. Text encoder placement.** `CLIPLoader -> device` can be set to `cpu`. Don't,\nunless you are OOMing during the encode - it pins 15.7 GB in system RAM permanently\nand runs a 32 B model on the CPU. Letting DynamicVRAM stream it is faster here."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Dials, in the order you should touch them\n\n**1. `steps` (Scheduler node).** Every step streams the full 21 GB DiT. Step count is\ndirectly proportional to wall-clock time. 20 is the quality default; 12-14 is fine for\nchecking framing and motion before committing.\n\n**2. `Duration`.** 2.0 s -> 56 frames. The math node snaps seconds *up* to H3's 17k+5\nframe grid at 24 fps, so the value you type is a request, not the result - only these\nlengths are reachable, and anything in between rounds up to the next one:\n\n| you set | frames | real length | latent T |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1.0 | 39 | 1.62 s | 12 |\n| 2.0 | 56 | 2.33 s | 17 |\n| 2.5 or 3.0 | 73 | 3.04 s | 22 |\n| 3.5 | 90 | 3.75 s | 27 |\n| 4.0 | 107 | 4.46 s | 32 |\n| 4.5 or 5.0 | 124 | 5.17 s | 37 |\n\n**3. `Resolution`.** Note this barely moves VRAM - the weights dominate, not the\nactivations. It moves *compute* time. H3 is trained on a 768 px short edge capped at\n768x1344, so going below 768 costs real quality for modest speed. Settings that land\nexactly on native canvases (keep `multiple` = 32):\n\n| aspect | megapixels | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1:1 | 0.56 | 768 x 768 (default here) |\n| 4:3 | 0.75 | 1024 x 768 |\n| 3:4 | 0.75 | 768 x 1024 |\n| 16:9 | 0.98 | 1344 x 768 |\n| 9:16 | 0.98 | 768 x 1344 |\n\n1344x768 at 5 s is the heavy end - ~37k tokens through the DiT. It fits in 8 GB but\nit is where you would first see an OOM if something else is on the GPU.\n\n**4. `Sigma Shift`.** 12.0 / 3.0 are exactly the model's built-in defaults, so the node\nis a no-op as wired. It is here purely so you have the knob. Lower `shift_video`\nfor tighter, less drifty motion.\n\n**5. Text encoder placement.** `CLIPLoader -> device` can be set to `cpu`. Don't,\nunless you are OOMing during the encode - it pins 15.7 GB in system RAM permanently\nand runs a 32 B model on the CPU. Letting DynamicVRAM stream it is faster here."
      },
